From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ole Algoritme <olealgoritme@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 20:57:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] nvk: ZCULL for DXVK depth buffers and reverse Z

Two things kept ZCULL from working for D3D11 through DXVK on GB20x:

1. DXVK gives every D3D11 depth texture VK_IMAGE_USAGE_TRANSFER_DST_BIT,
   and NVK only allocates ZCULL storage for depth images written by
   nothing but depth attachments.  Without storage ZCULL only works in
   render passes that clear depth; every pass that loads it (DXVK ends a
   render pass at each barrier, resolve and render target change) runs
   without.

   Allow TRANSFER_DST (with VK_SHARING_MODE_EXCLUSIVE) and, after a
   transfer writes such an image outside a render pass (a copy from a
   buffer or an image, a blit, a resolve, a depth resolve attachment) or
   after it is acquired from another queue, record an empty render pass
   that resets its stored ZCULL to the far value of its direction and
   stores it: a conservative state whatever the depth buffer holds, which
   the next render passes build up again.

2. SET_ZCULL_DIR_FORMAT was always ZDIR_LESS, so with reverse Z (clear to
   0.0, GREATER tests), which many D3D11 engines use, ZCULL never culled.

   ZCULL culls in one direction and stored ZCULL must be loaded with the
   direction it was stored with.  Choose the direction per image, once:
   the first render pass that records a ZCULL load or store on it picks
   GREATER for an application clear below 0.5 and LESS otherwise, and the
   image keeps it, so every LOAD_ZCULL matches its STORE_ZCULL whatever
   order command buffers are recorded and submitted in.
   vkCmdClearDepthStencilImage does not choose (DXVK clears every new
   depth image to 0.0), and a pass that chooses while loading depth resets
   ZCULL instead of loading it.  Render passes without ZCULL storage take
   the direction from their clear value.  DONT_CARE seeds the far value
   of the direction instead of 0.0.

vk_perf_bench (guest/nvk-rm/tests/perf in Conduit), RTX 5090, 2560x1440,
GPU ms, median of 11, NVIDIA 610.57.04 in brackets: 32 front-to-back
layers of a 16-iteration ALU shader over a depth image with DXVK's usage,
split over 8 render passes that load depth 0.162 -> 0.109 (0.102), over 2
passes 0.111 -> 0.078 (0.079); the same in one pass with reverse Z 0.141
-> 0.070 (0.071).  Everything else unchanged.  vk_perf_bench -t zcoh
(depth written by copies from a buffer and an image, a blit and
vkCmdClearDepthStencilImage between a cleared and a loading render pass,
both directions, and direction choice cases) passes; without the reset
after transfers the copy cases draw nothing.  Image hashes of the other
correctness tests are unchanged.
